{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"P1 FP ASSESSMENT: would the recommended surface-parity widening (content-triggered on CLI arg/guard changes + NDJSON/import channel) have yielded historical false positives?\n\nMETHOD (judgment + git evidence, no LLM replays, per operator ruling). Modeled criterion: fires when a commit's diff changes CLI argument/guard surfaces under src/rebar/_cli/ (heuristic: git log -G over add_argument|required=|choices=|--flag tokens), channels = MCP (src/rebar/_mcp_*, mcp_server.py) + NDJSON/import (src/rebar/_io/import_ndjson.py, export_ndjson.py). Window: 85 commits qualify over the last 60 days; sampled the 40 most recent (2026-07-30 -> 2026-08-21), the ~40-commit cap binding first. Ground truth per commit from the diff plus subsequent history (follow-up fixes, escaped-bug tickets).\n\nRESULTS — trigger count 40, split:\n- TP-class 4/40 (10%): the MCP surface genuinely owed a matching update and the commit did not discharge it — d1466ff18f (transition --reason semantics), 63db6ac5a8 (--force-close -> --force rename), 0f34e8dc3b (reason-required dispositions: made compliant closes UNREACHABLE over MCP), d8fac8981b (unified --force[=<reason>] on transition+claim). All four are ONE defect family that escaped as bug 1128-505b (\"MCP transition_ticket/claim_ticket lack reason/caused_by/ref/force parity\"), fixed 2026-08-18 (e9969f8aec).\n- Owed-and-discharged 8/40 (20%): parity updated in the same diff (32f2dd5f41, a22e6f3642, 710976dd2f, 694cf894de, ed0216f279, d21f2cb091, 31f352d535, 1fbfb5c691) — the criterion fires, verifies MIGRATED, emits nothing.\n- Not-owed 28/40 (70%) = the FP-exposure pool: the trigger fires but no MCP/NDJSON obligation exists. Largest cluster: 6 RP-05 behavior-preserving parser/help-factory refactors (22efd71f10 alone rewrites 75 CLI files with zero semantic arg change). Plus 9 bridge/maintenance CLI-only verbs (fsck/doctor/tracker-maintenance/bridge pause/status/preview), guards living in shared core below all surfaces (ac3f6c1e60, e2bb6b3840), CLI-only UX (42cd70b889, d7d7594305), and — pointedly — 9844f6de35 (admin close dispositions), a named Sample-A origin commit: even the WIDENED channel list misses its real siblings (gates.py, a help .txt, spawn sites), while MCP/NDJSON owed nothing (close_class pass-through already threaded 2026-07-19).\n\nCorroboration outside the sample: 662d8db31e (2026-07-18, persist bug-close --class) replays the founding bug halfwhite-chordal-stonefly — MCP+NDJSON threading landed a day later as 0f5dbc88b9 (376d); fb76631573 (--ref) also waited until e9969f8aec. The widened trigger would have been TP on both.\n\nCOMPARISON vs the ~90%-'none' precedent (docs/plan-review-gate.md, omitted-scope-site class: 1,307 findings, ~90% graded none): the genuine-obligation density here is 10% of triggers — the same order as that class's ~10% non-none rate. With perfect UNCOVERED-only discipline the criterion would emit 4 findings/40 triggers at 0% FP; at precedent-like discipline over the 70% not-owed pool it converges on the ~90%-none FP profile. Nothing in this sample suggests this criterion would beat the precedent.\n\nDECISIVE POST-HOC FACT: every in-window TP belongs to a single class — write-parameter parity across library/CLI/MCP — which is now covered DETERMINISTICALLY: the bug-1128 fix (e9969f8aec, 2026-08-18) added the transport-agnostic write-parity oracle (tests/interfaces/write_parity_contract.py + test_write_parity_oracle.py): one contract table executed through all three adapters, PARAM_NOT_EXPOSED divergences fail the suite, known gaps are strict-xfails. The widened LLM criterion would have caught those 4 commits EARLIER, but going forward its entire demonstrated TP family is caught by CI at zero LLM cost. Residual uncovered channel: NDJSON/import is NOT one of the oracle's adapters; verified NDJSON-owing instances in the window: 1 (the founding --class bug).\n\nRECOMMENDATION: REJECT the content-triggered widening. 70% of triggers owe nothing, the precedent predicts an FP-dominated criterion, and its only demonstrated TP family is now deterministically tested. The cheap deterministic residual (consistent with the operator's P0/P3 posture of preferring deterministic checks over LLM criteria): extend the write-parity contract with an NDJSON/import adapter or import-schema parity rows. If any change to the surface-parity criterion is made at all, the only evidence-supported subset is appending the NDJSON/import channel to the EXISTING glob trigger; converting the trigger to content-based is not supported."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787353842219261001,"uuid":"bcecc54c-e56c-45aa-9b2c-fdd303908384"}